# Trivy ignore list for image vulnerability scanning.
#
# These are Debian/apt base-image OS package CVEs where a fixed package
# version exists upstream but is not yet present in the Debian mirror(s)
# used by our self-hosted runner at build time. `apt-get upgrade` in the
# Dockerfile already picks up fixes as soon as the mirror has them, so
# these entries are a transient allowance, not a permanent exception.
#
# Review/remove entries periodically (see date next to each CVE). If a
# CVE is still listed after its review date, re-check whether the fix is
# now available and remove the entry, or renew the note with a reason.

# libssl3t64 3.5.6-1~deb13u2 -> fixed in 3.5.7-1~deb13u2 (not yet in mirror)
# added 2026-08-26, review by 2026-09-26
CVE-2026-14456
